## Phase 7 — Ambient Occlusion

**Goal:** Add contact grounding and local depth without ray tracing.

Current implementation is a GTAO-style screen-space pass that reuses the opaque depth prepass and a world-normal target. AO is computed and depth/normal-aware filtered on SDL_GPU compute, then supplied to PBR through a graphics storage buffer. It modulates diffuse GI/ambient contribution only; it does not incorrectly darken direct light. Camera-layer/viewmodel geometry does not consume world AO.

